course: dictionary
lesson: 9264
title: Words for direction
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Southward is a direction word. It tells you which way something moves: towards the south. The ending -ward means "in the direction of", like forward or homeward.
explain: «The explorers sailed southward, towards the icy lands near Antarctica.» The word sailed tells you a ship was moving, and southward tells you the way. You can check your meaning by swapping it in: "sailed towards the south" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Maps help too. On most maps, south is at the bottom of the page. So when something moves southward, it moves down the map.
fact: Southward means towards the south.
fact: Southward can be an adjective, as in a southward journey, or an adverb, as in birds flying southward. Southwards means the same thing.
fact: On a map, south is usually at the bottom, so southward means moving down the map.
fact: Many birds migrate southward in autumn in the Northern Hemisphere to find warmer weather and food.
fact: Explorers have sailed southward towards Antarctica, the cold land at the bottom of the world.
exercise: Which way does southward mean? | Towards the north | Towards the east | Towards the sky | *Towards the south
exercise: On a map, which way does southward take you? | Off the edge of the map | Up to the top of the page | Round in a circle | *Down to the bottom of the page
exercise: «The explorers sailed southward towards the ice.» Find and copy the word that tells you the direction. | explorers | sailed | *southward | ice
test: Why do many birds fly southward in autumn? | Because they want to sleep all winter | Because the sea is too cold to cross | *To find warmer weather and food | To visit the north pole for fun
test: Which sentence uses southward correctly? | The cat slept southward on the mat | The song was southward and loud | The bread was southward and warm | *The geese turned southward when the cold weather came
exam: «The geese turned southward when the cold came.» What does southward mean? | Towards the sky | Towards the sea | *Towards the south | Towards the north
